          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is egg white protein as good as whey for building muscle?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Very nearly. Both are complete, highly digestible animal proteins. Egg has a little less leucine, roughly 8 to 9 percent of its protein against 10 to 11 percent for whey, so take about 30 g of egg protein instead of 25 g if you want to match whey. Total daily protein and consistent training matter far more than the source.
